title:: MIR2 legacy migration
summary:: Moving from historical SuperCollider analyzers to MIR2
categories:: Libraries>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2

MIR2 successors preserve the musical purpose of historical analyzers, not their exact numbers or defaults. Keep the old and new analyzer side by side while migrating a piece, and recalibrate thresholds from documented units.

section:: Available in version 0.1

table::
## Legacy || MIR2 || Main intentional difference
## link::Classes/SpecCentroid:: || link::Classes/SpecCentroid2:: || Explicit Hz bounds and magnitude/power weighting.
## link::Classes/SpecFlatness:: || link::Classes/SpecFlatness2:: || Stable logarithmic floor and defined silence result.
## link::Classes/SpecPcile:: || link::Classes/SpecPcile2:: || General fraction and optional within-bin interpolation.
## link::Classes/MFCC:: || link::Classes/MFCC2:: || Configurable bands, coefficient zero, Mel mapping, DCT, and no historical output normalization.
## link::Classes/FFTFlux:: / link::Classes/FFTFluxPos:: || link::Classes/FFTFlux2:: || One explicit distance interface with normalized/full/positive modes.
## link::Classes/Onsets:: || link::Classes/Onsets2:: || Trigger plus continuous strength and a causal SuperFlux-style method.
## link::Classes/Pitch:: || link::Classes/Pitch2:: || YIN/MPM, explicit confidence and octave ambiguity, no default stale-frequency hold.
## link::Classes/Tartini:: || link::Classes/PitchMPM:: || Independent paper-based MPM with explicit frames, hops, clarity, and silence.
::

section:: Important argument changes

MIR2 FFT analyzers require code::fftSize:: to match their chain. This lets stateful analyzers allocate all frame memory during construction. code::Onsets2:: also requires code::hop:: to match code::FFT:: so its seconds-based history remains correct.

MIR2 pitch code::frameSize:: and code::hop:: replace the execution-frequency and downsampling assumptions used by some historical trackers. Frequency becomes zero on failed voicing unless code::Pitch2.kr(..., hold: 1):: is requested.

section:: Planned names

The longer MIR2 plan proposes further code::*2:: successors, but unimplemented names are deliberately absent from version 0.1. This prevents a placeholder from being mistaken for a verified analyzer.

